  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I made a Spleef game in vrchat, and there is a lot going on in terms of network updates with obj sync(animations and triggers).  I have to reset 765 box colliders and mesh renderers when the game finishes.  The issue is that the host of the world becomes frozen in place for everyone around them.  The host can still move their own avatar, but everyone else sees them stuck in place.  They can still be heard from other players near them too.  I think the reason for this is because there is a lot of network traffic that the host has to process in order for things to sync up for all players.  All of the resets are set to always unbuffered.  What I am currently doing is a set of 6 on enable triggers that have a spaced out delay of 6 seconds to reset chunks of the blocks.  I was wondering if there was a fix for this or if there is a better way to go about what I am doing here.  You can test what I am saying here: https://www.vrchat.net/home/launch?worldId=wrld_979c3ab1-65a9-4b2e-ac3f-f963dbc0008d&instanceId=64221~hidden(usr_fc6ab45a-fb05-4284-be3a-42664d1421dc)~nonce(874eda36-64e3-4605-900a-2506de92f762)",
